1
00:00:00,249 --> 00:00:02,379
(Raj:)Sheldon,
we've been on this train 90 seconds...

2
00:00:02,543 --> 00:00:04,793
(Leonard:)...and you've already said
a thousand words.

3
00:00:04,962 --> 00:00:07,802
(Leonard:)Just tell us where to sit and shut up.

4
00:00:09,842 --> 00:00:11,222
(Sheldon(ripping off sticker):)Here.

5
00:00:11,385 --> 00:00:14,055
(Sheldon:)I'm hoping once you reap
the endorphic rewards...

6
00:00:14,221 --> 00:00:17,391
(Sheldon:)...of the steady clickety-clack
of steel wheels on polished rails...

7
00:00:17,558 --> 00:00:20,558
(Sheldon:)- ...your sour disposition will abate.
- Yeah, maybe.

8
00:00:20,728 --> 00:00:26,068
(Leonard:)Back in the 21st century, people are raising
tray tables and putting seat-backs upright...

9
00:00:26,233 --> 00:00:29,233
...because it's time to land
in San Francisco.

10
00:00:29,570 --> 00:00:32,740
(Raj:)It's not so bad really.
At least these trains have modern plumbing.

11
00:00:32,906 --> 00:00:36,576
(Raj:)In India, you squat over a hole in the train
and expose your naked buttocks...

12
00:00:36,744 --> 00:00:38,574
(Raj:)...to the chilly air of Rajasthan.

13
00:00:39,246 --> 00:00:41,336
(Sheldon:)He is referring, of course, to third class...

14
00:00:41,498 --> 00:00:44,168
(Sheldon:)...on Indian Railways' magnificent
Ranakpur Express...

15
00:00:44,335 --> 00:00:48,885
...and its 1200-kilometer journey
from Maharashtra to the Bikaner Junction.

16
00:00:49,048 --> 00:00:51,838
(Leonard:)Oh, look.
Now he's boring on an international scale.

17
00:00:53,594 --> 00:00:56,264
Holy crap, look.

18
00:00:57,765 --> 00:01:00,095
- Is that who I think it is?
- It can't be.

